+
+| Finding | Activities | Identity process/evidence | Transfer to measurements and other overlays |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Continuing identity and continuing source positions are separate decisions | D, M, R | A captured survivor manifest maps prior occurrence indices to new exact spans; g01 keeps its UUID/binding while losing one reference. Exact slice checks do not decide whether its meaning continues | A measurement or observation can keep its logical ID while row/text positions change, but retaining that ID requires an explicit domain continuity decision |
+| A partial record update needs explicit empty-record retirement | D, P, M | g02's empty survivor list removes the saved group/resolution/declaration; native source removal plus generated-retention cleanup removes its unowned node/vector/markers. Tests require absence, not only new output presence | Removing the last supporting observation must retire that source's declarations and materialization, while preserving objects retained by other sources |
